From: Sirius port
Subject: [PATCH 10/12] clk: qcom: hfpll: add msm8974 HFPLL data

The binding (Documentation/devicetree/bindings/clock/qcom,hfpll.yaml)
documents qcom,msm8974-hfpll, but the driver has no match entry for it, so an
msm8974 device tree can only use the deprecated "qcom,hfpll" compatible,
which selects the qcs404 data: config_val 0x430405d and a 1248 MHz low-VCO
boundary. Those are wrong for this PLL and would be written to the config
register at the first rate change.

Sony's stock device tree for the Xperia Z2 gives the correct values on its
qcom,clock-krait@f9016000 node:

	qcom,hfpll-config-val    = <0x4d0405d>;
	qcom,hfpll-user-vco-mask = <0x100000>;

Register offsets are the standard Krait HFPLL layout, unchanged from the
other supported parts.

min_rate, max_rate and low_vco_max_rate match Qualcomm's downstream 8974
clock driver (drivers/clk/qcom/clock-krait-8974.c, hdata): 537.6 MHz,
2.9 GHz, and a 1248 MHz low-VCO boundary. The config value there comes from
the device tree, and 0x04d0405d reads back live from all five HFPLL config
registers on a running Z2.

--- a/drivers/clk/qcom/hfpll.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/qcom/hfpll.c
@@ -14,6 +14,24 @@
 #include "clk-regmap.h"
 #include "clk-hfpll.h"
 
+static const struct hfpll_data msm8974 = {
+	.mode_reg = 0x00,
+	.l_reg = 0x04,
+	.m_reg = 0x08,
+	.n_reg = 0x0c,
+	.user_reg = 0x10,
+	.config_reg = 0x14,
+	.config_val = 0x4d0405d,
+	.status_reg = 0x1c,
+	.lock_bit = 16,
+
+	.user_val = 0x8,
+	.user_vco_mask = 0x100000,
+	.low_vco_max_rate = 1248000000,
+	.min_rate = 537600000UL,
+	.max_rate = 2900000000UL,
+};
+
 static const struct hfpll_data qcs404 = {
 	.mode_reg = 0x00,
 	.l_reg = 0x04,
@@ -84,6 +102,7 @@
 };
 
 static const struct of_device_id qcom_hfpll_match_table[] = {
+	{ .compatible = "qcom,msm8974-hfpll", .data = &msm8974 },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,msm8976-hfpll-a53", .data = &msm8976_a53 },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,msm8976-hfpll-a72", .data = &msm8976_a72 },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,msm8976-hfpll-cci", .data = &msm8976_cci },
